"""Render the nine fixed paper-design cases, not runtime question generation."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
import sympy as sp
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];W=P.parent;t=sp.symbols('t');cases=json.loads((P/'d2/motion-cases.json').read_text());lines=['# Motion — D2 fixed paper exemplars','','Recipe `WB8227-motion-integration@0.1.2`; classification `8227-pilot-design-0.1.1`. Newly authored Stage-D designs. Claude confirmation then Vitalis approval pending; no runtime items. Exact or 3 significant figures, decimal half-up. D1-MR01–09 and the work-order dependencies apply. All parts require visible evidence.']
L=lambda expr:sp.latex(sp.sympify(expr,locals={'t':t}))
for c in cases:
 p=c['parameters'];a=c['expected_answers'];slug=c['branch_id'].split(':')[-1];lines+=['',f'## {slug}: {c["case_role"]}','','Author parameters (internal): `'+json.dumps(p)+'`. Total '+str(c['mark_total'])+' marks.']
 if slug=='polynomial-chain':
  A,B,u,T=[p[k]for k in ['A','B','u','T']];v=A*t*t+B*t+u;acc=2*A*t+B;primitive=sp.Rational(A,3)*t**3+sp.Rational(B,2)*t*t+u*t;dist=sp.Rational(a['distance']);dec=format(float(dist),'.3g');decimal_label='exact' if dist.q==1 else '3 s.f.'
  lines+=['',f'Stem: A particle passes O at t=0 with velocity {u} m/s. Its acceleration is ${L(acc)}$ m/s². (a) Find velocity in terms of t, showing integration and the initial condition. [3] (b) Find distance travelled in the first {T} seconds, in metres, showing working. Exact or 3 significant figures. [3]','','| Action | Reason | Result |','|---|---|---|',f'| Integrate acceleration | Acceleration is dv/dt | $v={L(A*t*t+B*t)}+C$ |',f'| Impose v(0)={u} | Initial velocity fixes the integration constant | $C={u}$, so $v={L(v)}$ |',f'| Integrate v, evaluate both bounds | v is positive throughout, so travelled distance equals displacement | $[{L(primitive)}]_0^{{{T}}}={L(dist)}$ m, or {dec} m ({decimal_label}) |','','V1–V3 and S1–S3 give 6/6. S3 depends on S1 and S2. A correct value from differentiating velocity or a calculator, without the required integration, earns no S3. A missing initial constant loses V3; visible integration of their velocity can retain S1/S2 but not canonical S3. A bare answer earns zero; practice recognises value correctness and asks for evidence.']
 elif slug=='exponential-positive':
  V,k,T=p['V'],sp.Rational(p['k']),p['T'];v=V*sp.exp(-k*t);acc=-k*v;prim=-V/k*sp.exp(-k*t)
  lines+=['',f'Stem: The particle has velocity $v={L(v)}$ m/s. (a) Find acceleration at time t, showing differentiation. [2] (b) Find distance travelled in the first {T} seconds in metres, showing integration and boundary evaluation; exact or 3 significant figures. [3]','','| Action | Reason | Result |','|---|---|---|',f'| Differentiate the velocity | The chain multiplier is ${L(-k)}$ and the exponential index stays unchanged | $a={L(acc)}$ m/s² |',f'| Integrate velocity | Integration needs the reciprocal chain factor | $F(t)={L(prim)}$ |',f'| Evaluate F({T})−F(0) | Velocity stays positive; both bounds matter | $d={L(a["distance_exact"])}$ m = {a["distance_3sf"]} m (3 s.f.) |','','E1–E5 give 5/5. Alternatively determine an integration constant from d(0)=0, then evaluate at T; fill the same awards, do not add them. A primitive coefficient used as a derivative is excluded at E2. Bounds substituted into the original velocity/derivative do not earn E4. Omitting the lower boundary retains E3 alone. Misreading V=12 as21 coherently retains structural E2 and method E4, but loses value-bearing E1/E3 and canonical E5:2/5 under the shared rule.']
 else:
  k,r,cc,T=[p[x]for x in ['k','r','c','T']];v=sp.expand(k*(t-r)*(t+cc));primitive=sp.sympify(a['primitive'],locals={'t':t});roots=a['roots'];inside=a['interior_roots'];desc=f'Only {r} lies inside the interval; signs change there'if inside else f'Both roots lie outside (0,{T}); v stays '+('positive'if k<0 else'negative')+' throughout'
  lines+=['',f'Stem: A particle has velocity $v={L(v)}$ m/s for $0\\le t\\le {T}$, with the positive direction stated. (a) Find total distance travelled in metres and justify your working. [4] (b) Find signed displacement in metres, showing working; exact or 3 significant figures. [2] Neither title nor stem tells the learner whether direction changes.','','| Action | Reason | Result |','|---|---|---|',f'| Solve v=0 and compare roots with the interval | Decide whether distance needs one or two sign-constant legs | Roots {roots}; {desc} |',f'| Integrate the expanded velocity | Quadratic velocity needs a cubic primitive; endpoint triangles are not exact | $F(t)={L(primitive)}$ |',f'| Evaluate each selected leg with both bounds | Travelled length adds nonnegative leg magnitudes | Signed legs '+', '.join('$'+L(x)+'$ m'for x in a['signed_legs'])+f'; distance ${L(a["distance"])}$ m |',f'| Add signed legs, or integrate over the complete interval | Displacement retains direction rather than taking magnitudes | ${L(a["displacement"])}$ m |','','Distance earns R1–R4=4/4; displacement R5/R6=2/2. R1 allows one slip in a visible root solve followed by a coherent interval/sign check. R3 follows through that credible root only with an attempted primitive and both bounds. R4 depends on correct R2 and valid R3. A root check plus numerical quadrature legs without a primitive earns R1 only. Reusing the part-(a) primitive or adding its signed evaluated legs is valid for R5. A guessed split or an unchecked |net integral| cannot stand in for R1/R3 even if its value coincides.']
 lines+=['','Independent recomputation: `planning/d2/motion-design-check.json` uses separate CAS differentiation/integration and root isolation, with numerical quadrature for the mixed branch. All exact outputs agree. This is author verification, not independent acceptance or runtime marking.']
(W/'exemplars/WB8227-motion-integration.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
